galaxyxr-mini-tools (2~26.10.1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Create device-mapper names as symlinks to the kernel nodes, allowing
    udev to take over mappings created before it starts.
  * Mark resume events as device-mapper activations so udev also handles
    mappings created on a running system without a vendor-specific rule.
  * Atomically replace dangling mapper links and matching legacy block nodes
    when creating a mapping, while preserving unrelated paths.

